            "kind": "REWORK",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "configurations/platform/amd/helios_vulcano_800g_ocp_nic_server.json",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "Why is this in a new \"platform\" directory?  Can we just put it in `configurations/amd`?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "configurations/platform/amd/helios_vulcano_800g_ocp_nic_server.json",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "andychung113",
                        "email": "andy.chung@amd.com",
                        "username": "andychung113"
                    },
                    "message": "To follow https://gerrit.openbmc.org/c/openbmc/entity-manager/+/85991, put the platform config under \"platform\" directory."
                },
                {
                    "file": "configurations/platform/amd/helios_vulcano_800g_ocp_nic_server.json",
                    "line": 171,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "What is this?\n\nThis seems like any system with your NIC plugged into it that happens to have two boards with this name is going to load your config.  That doesn't seem appropriate."
                },
                {
                    "file": "configurations/platform/amd/helios_vulcano_800g_ocp_nic_server.json",
                    "line": 171,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "andychung113",
                        "email": "andy.chung@amd.com",
                        "username": "andychung113"
                    },
                    "message": "In the system design, BE NIC should be plugged into Helios EAM, so it's better to add EAM FRU here.\nHowever, in the early development stage, we do not have enough EAM, this should be temporary probe condition to enable engineer samples that without EAM. \nOr should we just put this patch in META downstream project layer as a short-term solution?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "configurations/platform/amd/helios_vulcano_800g_ocp_nic_server.json",
                    "line": 171,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "Can we start with an EM config for the NIC itself?  We can then talk about how to adjust the \"platform\" pieces here but since platforms themselves aren't merged yet and the MCTPUSB stuff isn't merged yet, it seems like this is a ways out from getting merged.  If you at least add a config for the base FRU we at least get inventory from it."
                }
            ],
